import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 668 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 669 | 2026-10-26 | **Listen, Clap, Write, chapter 29 (Build AE; the syllabus check's 'Ears for Grade 1').** Built on row 668. The second aural room, at the end of the second Prelim - Grade 1 floor; on the Home it joins the Aural door after Listen and sing (thArea counts it as aural). The Grade 1 aural tests and the theory's listening, one step each, with pads: (1) The home note: a short tune in C or G position stops on 2 or 5; hum home, tap it on the keys, the tune resolves (the position is named only afterwards). (2) Two or three? oom-pah or oom-pah-pah (the low note on 1, the chord on the others), 'Which one?'. (3) Clap it back: four bars in 2/4 or 3/4, heard twice (each with its count-in), then tapped with the clicks; scored on time; the notes show only afterwards. (4) Sing it with its rhythm: a phrase with walks, run-nings and a held note, heard twice, sung on 'la', then played in C position. (5) Write the rhythm: two bars of crotchets and minims in 2/4 or 3/4 (no dots, rests or anacrusis, as the theory asks), built note by note with a 1-beat and a 2-beat button, up to five hearings, checked against the answer. Drill: six heard levels (find the home note, two or three, which rhythm, which shape, clap it back, write the rhythm); no printed worksheet. Book: 7 pages. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch693.py (+ lwx.jsx, lwh.jsx). |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
